Content
Brainstorming & Idea Prioritization
1. Project Background

The project focuses on improving record security in ServiceNow by controlling access to institution records based on user roles and the value of the Branch field.

2. Problems Identified
Unauthorized users may access institution records.
Users may access records belonging to branches they are not authorized to view.
Different users require different permissions for different operations.
Administrators require complete access to manage the system.
Standard access control may not provide sufficient field-based record restrictions.
3. Ideas Considered

The following ideas were considered during brainstorming:

Role-based access control.
Branch-based record restriction.
Script-controlled Access Control Lists.
Separate ACLs for READ, CREATE, WRITE, and DELETE operations.
Administrator access for complete system management.
4. Selected Project Idea

The selected idea is:

Script-Controlled ACL – Restrict Record Access Based on Field Value

The solution uses ServiceNow ACLs and scripts to control access to institution records according to user roles and the Branch field.

5. Reason for Selection

The idea was selected because it provides:

Better control over record access.
Branch-based security.
Separate permissions for different operations.
Improved protection of institution information.
Full access for administrators.
6. Expected Benefits
Prevent unauthorized record access.
Protect institution information.
Control READ, CREATE, WRITE, and DELETE operations.
Improve data security.
Provide a structured and maintainable access-control mechanism
